    ],
    "source_pages": [
      29
    ],
    "text": "Our calculations also show that it is hard for a private company to make pro\ufb01t in the near future, but there truly exist opportunities to make money sev- eral decades after. According to our model, the debris threat now is at a low level and the increasing rate of debris is at a low level. But the turning point will occur after about 50 years when debris start to grow exponentially and collision between spacecraft and debris become increasingly frequent. At that time, O- DR may begins to make money through \ufb01nance from government or companies that own satellites."
  },
